("ul", ["Shape, size and sharpness depend on where the object is relative to the source and the screen.", "A shadow may or may not reveal what the object is.", "With the torch close to the object the shadow is larger; with the torch far, smaller. Two torches give two shadows.", "A bird high in the sky has a tiny, faint shadow on the ground; near the ground its shadow is clear. The length of your shadow is shortest at noon, when the Sun is highest.", "**Shadow play** (shadow puppetry) is a traditional art: Charma Bahuli Natya (Maharashtra), Tholu Bommalata and Keelu Bomme (Andhra Pradesh), Togalu Gombeyaata (Karnataka), Ravana Chhaya (Odisha), Tholpavakoothu (Kerala), Bommalattam (Tamil Nadu)."]),
